# Force text classification on TS/TSX source files so git diff never
# treats them as binary even when a stray control byte (escaped string
# literal, \x07-like) lands in the source. Without this, git's auto-
# detection sticks "binary" on the file across subsequent commits;
# diffs show "Bin" instead of actual changes, breaking code review.
#
# Triggered after commit ba30f33 (terminal layouts handler test) which
# accidentally landed with literal NULL + 0x1F bytes from a copy-paste.
# Cleanup commit 8e877e7 stripped the bytes but git kept the binary
# attribute; this .gitattributes is the proper fix.
*.ts text
*.tsx text
*.js text
*.jsx text
*.json text
*.md text
*.sql text
*.css text
*.html text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
